cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Censura: Black++ - The Enhanced Python Code Formatter"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Langa
    given-names: Łukasz
  - name: "contributors to Black (forked as Censura)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kactlabs/censura"
url: "https://censura.readthedocs.io/en/stable/"
abstract: >-
  Censura is an enhanced Python code formatter built on Black's foundation. It extends
  Black's uncompromising approach with additional features and improvements, delivering
  the same speed and determinism you expect, plus more. Censura maintains Black's core
  philosophy while adding powerful enhancements for modern Python development.

  Like Black++, Censura produces consistent, readable code that looks the same across
  projects, letting you focus on what matters: writing great code, not formatting it.
license: MIT
